---
<DocPage eyebrow="DOCS / .NET PACKAGES" title=".NET packages" lead="Core and Testing provide the shared base. Add the shared Runtime, Godot or Unity host, PNG comparison, semantic snapshots, or semantic Recording only where needed." description="Reference for Gua Core, Runtime, Testing, Godot, Unity, Visual, Snapshots, Recording, and their target frameworks." section="docs">
  <h2>Install</h2><CodeBlock title="Add only the features you need" lang="powershell" code={`dotnet add package Gua.Core --version 1.1.0\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing --version 1.1.0\n\n# Implement an engine adapter\ndotnet add package Gua.Runtime --version 1.1.0\n\n# Launch an engine process from an external test\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing.Godot --version 1.1.0\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing.Unity --version 1.1.0\n\n# Optional capabilities\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing.Visual --version 1.1.0\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing.Snapshots --version 1.1.0\ndotnet add package Gua.Testing.Recording --version 1.1.0`} /><p>The examples pin 1.1.0. Keep the game integration and all Gua packages in one project on the same version. <code>Visual</code>, <code>Snapshots</code>, and <code>Recording</code> are independent opt-ins.</p>
  <p>NuGet: <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Core">Core</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing">Testing</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing.Godot">Testing.Godot</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing.Unity">Testing.Unity</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Runtime">Runtime</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing.Visual">Testing.Visual</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing.Snapshots">Testing.Snapshots</a> · <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Gua.Testing.Recording">Testing.Recording</a></p>
  <h2>Choose a package</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Add</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Write ordinary semantic UI tests</td><td><code>Gua.Testing</code> + engine host</td><td>Visibility, enabled state, text, values, and state transitions after actions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Build a custom engine adapter</td><td><code>Gua.Runtime</code></td><td>Publish semantic frames and implement actions, screenshots, and the Inspector bridge in the game.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detect rendering regressions</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.Visual</code></td><td>Find clipping, layout shifts, wrong assets or themes, and unexpected overlays.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detect semantic regressions</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.Snapshots</code></td><td>Compare IDs, hierarchy, text, values, state, and publication order with a JSON baseline.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Save and replay an interaction</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.Recording</code></td><td>Share regression flows, bug reproductions, and long journeys using semantic targets.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h2>Target frameworks</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>net10.0</th><th>netstandard2.1</th><th>Primary use</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Core</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>C ABI bindings for native Gua</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Locators, waits, assertions, and diagnostics</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Runtime</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Shared runtime C ABI wrapper for engine adapters</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing.Unity</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Build, launch, and connect Unity Editor/Players</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing.Visual</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>PNG baseline comparison</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing.Snapshots</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Semantic UI and optional World JSON baselines</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing.Recording</code></td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>Semantic action recording and replay</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Gua.Testing.Godot</code></td><td>✓</td><td>—</td><td>Control a Godot process from an external .NET test</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <Callout kind="tip" title=".NET Standard 2.1 support"><p><code>Gua.Core</code>, <code>Gua.Runtime</code>, <code>Gua.Testing</code>, <code>Gua.Testing.Unity</code>, <code>Gua.Testing.Visual</code>, <code>Gua.Testing.Snapshots</code>, and <code>Gua.Testing.Recording</code> target both <code>net10.0</code> and <code>netstandard2.1</code>. <code>Gua.Testing.Godot</code> targets <code>net10.0</code> only.</p></Callout>
  <h2>Gua.Core</h2><p>The lowest .NET layer over the native C ABI. It defines the UI-tree, request, and event contracts.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>IGuaContext</code></td><td>The common operation boundary shared by local and remote contexts.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaContext</code></td><td>Owns a native Gua context and its nodes, snapshots, requests, and events.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaSelector</code></td><td>Represents selection by ID, role, text, state, and scope.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaNodeState</code></td><td>Observed state such as visible, enabled, value, focused, and checked.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaAction</code> / <code>GuaEvent</code></td><td>An external request and the result or event observed by the host.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaReset</code></td><td>The contract for session epochs and clearing requests, events, and retained history.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h2>Gua.Runtime</h2><p><code>Gua.Runtime</code> is for managed engine-adapter authors, not ordinary test authors. It exposes the shared <code>gua_runtime</code> C ABI through typed APIs so adapters do not duplicate P/Invoke declarations, request queues, screenshot timeout handling, version publication, or Inspector WebSocket hosting. Choose it when integrating an engine other than Godot or Unity, or when adapting a custom UI framework. See the <a href="/docs/gua-runtime/">Gua.Runtime implementation guide</a>.</p>
  <Callout kind="tip" title="Ordinary tests do not reference it directly"><p>If you only use Gua from a Unity or Godot game or external test, reference the engine package or <code>Gua.Testing.*</code>. Add <code>Gua.Runtime</code> directly only when implementing the game-side adapter itself.</p></Callout>
  <h2>Gua.Testing.Unity</h2><p><code>UnityPlayerBuilder</code> and <code>UnitySceneTestHost</code> connect external tests to Unity 6 desktop Mono Players on Windows x64, Linux x64, Intel macOS, and Apple Silicon macOS, or to Editor Play Mode. Native Intel macOS Editor support is implemented but unverified. Use the host for Unity executable discovery, free-port allocation, bridge connection, and startup/teardown log capture. See the <a href="/docs/unity-reference/">Unity API reference</a> and <a href="/docs/release-1-1-0/#support">support limits</a>.</p>
  <h2>Gua.Testing</h2><p>Adds the higher-level API consumed by tests.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>GuaAssertions</code></td><td>Entry point for <code>GetById</code>, <code>GetByRole</code>, and <code>WaitFor...</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaLocatorQuery</code></td><td>Builds selectors with ByRole, ByText, Within, WhereVisible, and related filters.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaNodeSnapshot</code></td><td>Evidence for a node at the exact frame and revision where a wait succeeded.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaTestSession</code></td><td>Controls reset and strict leak detection around a test.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaAssertionScope</code></td><td>Applies framework failure handling and diagnostic options within a scope.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaDiagnostics</code></td><td>Writes the UI tree, logs, history, and environment metadata after a failure.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h2>Gua.Testing.Godot</h2><p>Starts a Godot process and connects to its in-game WebSocket bridge.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>GodotSceneTestHost</code></td><td>Owns scene startup, bridge connection, shutdown, process output, and screenshot access.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GodotSceneTestHostOptions</code></td><td>Configures the executable, project path, headless mode, port, environment, and reset policy.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaRemoteContext</code></td><td>An <code>IGuaContext</code> that polls snapshots and sends actions over WebSocket.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaRemoteUiTree</code></td><td>Converts a remote JSON snapshot into the .NET node model.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>GuaScreenshot</code></td><td>Represents a saved PNG, including its absolute path and dimensions.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <h2>Gua.Testing.Visual</h2><p>An opt-in layer for comparing explicitly captured PNGs with reviewed baselines. A semantic assertion may prove that a button is visible while missing that it is clipped, overlapping another control, using the wrong asset, or covered by an unexpected overlay. Visual testing closes that gap. It supports pixel thresholds, allowed difference ratios, masks, explicit OS/renderer variants, and dimension mismatch detection. See the <a href="/visual-testing/">visual testing guide</a> for setup and CI policy.</p>
  <CodeBlock title="Compare a screen with its baseline" lang="csharp" code={`var result = await GuaVisualAssertions.ExpectScreenshotAsync(\n    host.Context, "title-screen", new()\n    {\n        BaselineDirectory = "baselines",\n        ArtifactDirectory = "artifacts/gua",\n        BaselineVariant = "windows-unity-mono",\n        PixelThreshold = 0.02f,\n        MaxDifferentPixelRatio = 0.001,\n    });`} />
  <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Failure reason</th><th>Files written</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>pixel_difference</code></td><td><code>expected.png</code>, <code>actual.png</code>, <code>diff.png</code>, and <code>comparison.json</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>baseline_missing</code></td><td><code>actual.png</code> and <code>comparison.json</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>dimension_mismatch</code></td><td><code>expected.png</code>, <code>actual.png</code>, and <code>comparison.json</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p><code>comparison.json</code> records the comparison name, variant, actual dimensions, different-pixel metrics, thresholds, masks, failure reason, and diagnostic absolute <code>baselinePath</code>. The package does not generate HTML; the <a href="/docs/github-actions/#visual-report">gua-tester visual-report action</a> owns rendering and publication. Normal CI must not update its own baselines. Keep resolution, DPI, fonts, locale, theme, engine, and renderer deterministic, and mask only genuinely nondeterministic regions.</p>
  <h2 id="semantic-snapshots">Gua.Testing.Snapshots</h2><p>An independent opt-in layer that normalizes UI and optional World JSON before comparison with a baseline. <code>CompareSnapshot</code> returns a typed result; <code>ExpectSnapshot</code> throws an assertion exception carrying that result on failure. IDs, hierarchy, semantic properties, and array publication order remain significant. Geometry and runtime metadata are excluded by default; use Visual for PNG comparison.</p>
  <CodeBlock title="Compare a semantic baseline" lang="csharp" code={"using Gua.Testing.Snapshots;\n\nvar options = new SemanticSnapshotOptions\n{\n    BaselineDirectory = \"baselines/semantic\",\n    ArtifactDirectory = \"artifacts/semantic\",\n    BaselineVariant = \"english\",\n    Rules = new[]\n    {\n        new SemanticSnapshotRule(\"/ui/nodes/*/text\",\n            SemanticSnapshotRuleAction.Mask, \"account/name\"),\n    },\n};\nGuaSemanticSnapshots.ExpectSnapshot(host.Context, \"settings\", options);"} />
  <p>Missing baselines fail without creating one. Update explicitly with <code>UpdateBaselines = true</code> or exactly <code>GUA_UPDATE_SEMANTIC_BASELINES=1</code>. Keep updates disabled in regular CI and review baseline diffs before committing them. Visual's <code>GUA_UPDATE_BASELINES</code> does not approve semantic baselines.</p>
  <p>Configure mask/ignore rules before capture and cover every representation of sensitive data; there is no automatic secret detection. These rules do not redact screenshots or separate Trace observations. Each comparison retains <code>actual.json</code>, optional <code>expected.json</code>, <code>diff.json</code>, and <code>comparison.json</code>. An optional <code>WorldTreeProvider</code> is read sequentially with UI; callers must supply stable trees when a coordinated frame matters. See the <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/blob/gua-v1.1.0/bindings/dotnet/src/Gua.Testing.Snapshots/README.md">1.1.0 API and rule contract</a>.</p>
  <h2>Gua.Testing.Recording</h2><p>Stores multi-step journeys such as login, settings changes, or purchase confirmation as semantic actions for regression testing and bug reproduction. It records IDs and roles instead of coordinates, and waits for request-ID-correlated host completion on replay, making it more reliable than a fixed-delay macro. See the <a href="/recording/">recording guide</a> for complete workflows.</p>
  <CodeBlock title="Record and replay a journey" lang="csharp" code={`var recorder = new GuaRecorder(host.Context);\nawait recorder.ClickAsync(new(Id: "open-login"));\nawait recorder.SetValueAsync(new(Id: "password"), password,\n    sensitive: true, secretKey: "login-password");\nGuaRecordingFile.Save("recordings/login.json", recorder.Recording);\n\nvar recording = GuaRecordingFile.Load("recordings/login.json");\nawait GuaReplayer.ReplayAsync(host.Context, recording, new()\n{\n    SecretResolver = key => key == "login-password" ? password : null,\n});`} />
  <p><code>GuaRecorder</code>, <code>GuaReplayer</code>, and <code>GuaRecordingFile</code> support semantic wait conditions in place of fragile delays. Sensitive <code>set_value</code> steps store only a <code>secretKey</code>, never plaintext. Coordinate fallback is disabled by default.</p>
  <Callout kind="tip" title="Dependency direction"><p>The Unity game path is <code>Gua.Unity → Gua.Runtime → Gua.Core → native Gua</code>; the test path is <code>Gua.Testing.Unity → Gua.Testing → Gua.Core</code>. Visual, Snapshots, and Recording remain independent opt-ins.</p></Callout>
  <p>For package choices and Observe, Trace, lint, locator auto-wait, and distribution APIs, see <a href="/docs/release-1-1-0/">the package and feature guide</a>. Common Value C# APIs and the npm package are documented in <a href="/docs/value/">Value v1</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="extended-apis">Choose the API for the task</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Task</th><th>Package / API</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Read typed observations</td><td><code>Gua.Runtime</code> registration; <code>Gua.Testing.GuaWebSocketContext</code> subscriptions</td><td><a href="/docs/gua-runtime/#observe">Observe</a></td></tr><tr><td>Record test evidence and write offline HTML</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.GuaTraceSession</code> / <code>GuaTraceReport.WriteHtml</code></td><td><a href="/godot/testing/#trace">Trace</a></td></tr><tr><td>Check semantic structure</td><td><code>Gua.Core.GuaSemanticLinter.Analyze</code></td><td><a href="/semantic-ui-tree/#lint">Semantic lint</a></td></tr><tr><td>Query authorized physics</td><td><code>Gua.Runtime.GuaRuntimeSpatialClient</code>; <code>Gua.Testing.GuaWebSocketContext</code></td><td><a href="/world-object-tree/#physics">Spatial queries</a></td></tr><tr><td>Replay finite input offsets</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.Recording.GuaReplayer.ReplayTimedSegmentAsync</code></td><td><a href="/recording/#timed-segment">Timed Segment</a></td></tr><tr><td>Read packaged schemas offline</td><td><code>Gua.Testing.GuaDistribution.ReadSchema</code> / <code>ValidateJson</code></td><td><a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/blob/gua-v1.1.0/docs/distribution-contract.md">Resource API</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</DocPage>
